A||||3||JetroGT||Finding a car by the VIN?||||1||
Z||000000||JetroGT||02-24-2001||04:45 AM||||Is there a web site that I can go to, to find a specific fiero by using the vin #?<P>1G2PE11R2HP217043<BR>87 4cly auto. gold airconditioning.<P>I was able to get the vin # from one of the previous owners. The car has sentimental value to me. My girl friend used to own it and she was forced to get rid of it. Any help regarding this would be of great help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||02-24-2001||09:10 AM||||1 = made in USA<BR>G = General Motors<BR>2 = Pontiac<BR>PE = Fiero Coupe<BR>11 = Notchback<BR>R = 2.5l 4 cylinder engine<BR>2 = check digit<BR>H = 1987<BR>P = Pontiac, MI (GM plant it was assembled)<BR>217043 = plant sequence number<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 02-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||02-24-2001||12:08 PM||||If you know someone with an active carfax account they can check the VIN number and maybe get some idea what happened to it.<P>I checked last spring for the h-e-l-l of it on my old Camaro that I sold in late 1987, it had been inspected somewhere in the metro New York City area in early 2000 with nearly 170,000 miles on it. I liked that car but I needed a 4x4 and couldn't afford both, was kind of nice to know that someone else was still enjoying it.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||02-24-2001||01:16 PM||||Ok, I found you a good online VIN decoder at:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Vin/Default.asp?Version=81k45bs8" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Vin/Default.asp?Version=81k45bs8</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
